{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00456",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.9,
      "end_seconds": 2.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Hello, come through."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.57,
      "end_seconds": 4.27,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.66,
      "end_seconds": 6.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "So, busy day out there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.59,
      "end_seconds": 10.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Always is. The traffic coming in was terrible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.7,
      "end_seconds": 13.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "So, what's been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.13,
      "end_seconds": 16.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "I've been forgetting things lately."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.64,
      "end_seconds": 23.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "How long have you had it? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.93,
      "end_seconds": 45.43,
      "duration_seconds": 21.5,
      "text": "It's been about three months, I'm fairly sure. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. And I've been misplacing things as well, for six months. As for getting lost on familiar roads, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.62,
      "end_seconds": 50.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Alright, have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.12,
      "end_seconds": 65.98,
      "duration_seconds": 13.86,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.73,
      "end_seconds": 72.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Any low mood, hallucinations or weakness on one side at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.67,
      "end_seconds": 76.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Yeah, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.05,
      "end_seconds": 79.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Any falls or headache at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.56,
      "end_seconds": 81.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "No, no falls or headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.86,
      "end_seconds": 86.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.56,
      "end_seconds": 88.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.16,
      "end_seconds": 91.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.1,
      "end_seconds": 107.79,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "Not really, um, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.56,
      "end_seconds": 112.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.95,
      "end_seconds": 118.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Well, my father had a stroke. Okay, so my sister has thyroid problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.33,
      "end_seconds": 136.26,
      "duration_seconds": 15.93,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.76,
      "end_seconds": 140.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.42,
      "end_seconds": 144.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.73,
      "end_seconds": 150.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure. Yeah, you know, I've had diabetes, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.47,
      "end_seconds": 164.77,
      "duration_seconds": 13.3,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Yes, I can see the diabetes in your file as well. Alright, is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.85,
      "end_seconds": 169.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.69,
      "end_seconds": 172.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.73,
      "end_seconds": 178.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Um, yes, codeine. I get vomiting. Yes, sulfa drugs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.75,
      "end_seconds": 191.32,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.13,
      "end_seconds": 193.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.92,
      "end_seconds": 199.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.32,
      "end_seconds": 217.5,
      "duration_seconds": 15.18,
      "text": "Losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day. I take glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.69,
      "end_seconds": 220.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "One moment, I'm updating your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.18,
      "end_seconds": 242.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Right, carry on. Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.31,
      "end_seconds": 252.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.35,
      "end_seconds": 277.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 122 over 71, oxygen saturation is 97 percent. And temperature 36.6, pulse 67, respiratory rate 14."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.62,
      "end_seconds": 280.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.74,
      "end_seconds": 283.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.58,
      "end_seconds": 287.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.03,
      "end_seconds": 288.82,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.61,
      "end_seconds": 304.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Okay, here we go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.87,
      "end_seconds": 308.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.87,
      "end_seconds": 309.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.4,
      "end_seconds": 312.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.61,
      "end_seconds": 332.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Your gait is steady and the tone in your limbs is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.43,
      "end_seconds": 344.74,
      "duration_seconds": 10.31,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.98,
      "end_seconds": 350.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.94,
      "end_seconds": 351.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.19,
      "end_seconds": 394.62,
      "duration_seconds": 27.43,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with memory difficulties that need to be worked up at this stage. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. A vitamin deficiency is also on my list. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been forgetting things lately for about three months, and no weakness on one side or headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.91,
      "end_seconds": 398.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Yes, you know, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.88,
      "end_seconds": 404.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.51,
      "end_seconds": 415.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.92,
      "end_seconds": 424.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a CT scan of the head for memory loss. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 425.24,
      "end_seconds": 427.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "The earliest is Wednesday, 3:30 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.82,
      "end_seconds": 454.43,
      "duration_seconds": 25.61,
      "text": "We should do a vitamin B12 level for memory loss. Keep a daily routine and write things down, a notebook by the door works well. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Please come and see me in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 455.47,
      "end_seconds": 459.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 459.71,
      "end_seconds": 465.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 466.17,
      "end_seconds": 470.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "So, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 471.44,
      "end_seconds": 476.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 478.42,
      "end_seconds": 480.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Thanks so much, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 482.01,
      "end_seconds": 483.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}